/-!
# The exact-automorphism classes on `Fin 6`

`Definability/Structural.lean` turns structurality into `Aut(M') = Aut(M)`, so each conjugacy class
of subgroup of `S₆` is a rectangle of non-structurality facts: the laws with a model whose
automorphism group is *exactly* that subgroup are not structural over the laws with none.
This file is every class that is worth spending, `12` classes in all, one module each.

Everything here is generated by `genexact4.py` from the machinery in `Definability/ExactAut.lean`,
which explains the shape: a group `permE`, a set `permX` of permutations excluded to pin the group
down exactly, the orbits of the group on the `36` cells as `rep` and `tr`, and the invariant
operation `tab` written out cell by cell. `Magma.op_eq_transport` of
`Definability/Transport.lean` is the classification, and each orbit is indexed by the values its
stabilizer allows it, so the tuples enumerated are the invariant operations and not the whole
`n ^ m` space.  `mem` then lists the tuples whose automorphism group really is this group, and the
family is indexed by that list: an exactness test anywhere in the family definition would be re-run
at every table lookup, since a `Magma` is a bare closure, and that alone made these scans thousands
of times slower.

`Definability/Certs/Exact*.lean` record the rectangles.
-/
